# Every image in this monorepo builds with `context: ../..` (the repository root, see
# each project's docker-compose.yml) and then COPYs only the specific paths it needs --
# so this file is not what keeps unwanted files out of the final images. It exists for
# one load-bearing reason and one speed reason:
#
# Load-bearing: projects/pigrocrm/Dockerfile.web runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# for a Linux target *inside* the build stage, then COPYs the app directory. Without
# excluding node_modules here, that second COPY would pull in whatever node_modules
# already exists on the machine running `docker build` (this repository, right now,
# very likely has one from local development) and overwrite the freshly-installed
# Linux one with it. On a Mac or with a different pnpm store, that silently breaks the
# build on native-binary packages (esbuild, rollup, lightningcss, ...) with the wrong
# platform underneath -- confirmed by building without this exclusion first.
#
# Speed: everything else here just shrinks what gets sent to the Docker daemon as
# build context. That matters more now than it did before the monorepo, because the
# context is the whole repository and not one project.

.git
.env
.env.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

# Python
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# Node (see "Load-bearing" above)
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.tanstack/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime state that lives beside the checkout: PIGROCRM_DOCUMENTS_DIR's default, and
# either directory when an installation points it inside the checkout. Never wanted
# in an image, and large.
data/
var/

# Editor / tooling noise, and documentation no image reads
.superpowers/
.claude/
docs/
projects/*/docs/

# The print pieces (shared/brand/print/README.md): no image reads them, and a machine
# that renders them holds the business card's phone numbers in contacts.local.js.
shared/brand/print/
